Description: Offer a headless virtual output the 3D modes a monitor gets
 .
 A headless KWin (--virtual) has one 2D mode, so nothing could prove on it
 what only happens on a stereo output, such as a surface being told it may
 show depth inside it. With KWIN_VIRTUAL_STEREO_MODES=1 each virtual output
 also has the twins "Anaglyph" and "Other stereo formats" give a monitor
 (side by side half, top and bottom, anaglyph modern and CRT), so a saved
 configuration or the output management protocol can switch it into a 3D
 mode, as the integration tests do with their own modes. Without the variable
 nothing changes.
